{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_17019c432e9f8bc809006ca9fff6249fe47476d21ea0c28eac488000a7949651"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An optional agent-callable `boomerang` tool supports task mode (queued autonomous execution) and anchor mode (toggle a summary point); it is disabled by default and enabled via `/boomerang tool on`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1fdcd62eda1cd35372613ac2217abf4c758c41078eafa3d30fd7808a3ea190fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Boomerang summarizes only context/tokens and never touches file state; all file changes made during a task are preserved on disk."},{"claim_ids":["clm_25056fa832859cc129439995d0be008c159b1e980889b73c122d8f4409dac22f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"After completion, raw turn history is replaced in future context by an expanded handoff summary containing outcome, changed files, relevant reads, validation commands, failures, and config metadata."},{"claim_ids":["clm_599228afc967fef35c60dc291c2276814232ad73d8fbc79d8e49e699d6d39bd5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The session tree preserves full history for `/tree` navigation, so only future context is collapsed while the underlying history remains accessible."},{"claim_ids":["clm_68a38b2ae4350b2100afd876044ff55e730f624b7828240125278b2fd51ae4fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tool state and guidance persist to `~/.pi/agent/boomerang.json` across restarts, while anchor state is in-memory only and clears on session start or switch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7c4f251abe90fc57ca931b6a42d1457405259c7ab85deada8f915eeaca8e44cf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chained templates can be run in sequence (e.g. `/boomerang /scout -> /planner -> /impl`) with per-step inline args, global fallback args after `--`, and a single summary return at the end."},{"claim_ids":["clm_919899d9296e1b3b05f46285e769ee6489f9c48b201dd96bbcb061116870b5bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Template frontmatter fields `model`, `skill`, and `thinking` control each chain step's configuration, and boomerang restores the original config after the summary return."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c5dd72a4b88d678e304d363f3e66c996a75b77e8221c0d2e3892ca622e243e28"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`--rethrow N` (N required, 1-999) reruns the full task N times, summarizing between passes; file changes persist on disk and each pass sees accumulated summaries rather than raw history."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c9a8639ad875020b5e4a7caaace4436eda1afefcb8f7853c2ca752d6d82f4026"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented limitations: summaries are heuristic and may miss semantic details, the agent may still ask questions, anchor state is in-memory only, and tool-initiated summaries may lag in the UI until `/reload`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cc3fadac1a039620f9a1c7f171aa4de77e909eb14d2d484e590fc96b610f3a5a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The extension exposes a `/boomerang <task>` command that executes a task autonomously and summarizes context afterward, plus `/boomerang-cancel` to abort without summarizing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e0c6d478fe2aa23774b8688700c92310cceb9ed99265b213a2e13436287fb8ad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`--loop N` is treated as an alias for `--rethrow N`; if both flags are present `--rethrow` wins, loop metadata is stripped from rendered tasks, and bare `--loop` is invalid."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f9d977542e326a78296791841676d7ddb29eb2d09f6f9524ebef378f6558c443"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tasks starting with `/` are treated as prompt templates loaded from `<cwd>/.pi/prompts/` then `~/.pi/agent/prompts/`, with subdirectories mapping to path segments; `$@` and `$1`/`$2` expand args."}],"claim_ids":["clm_17019c432e9f8bc809006ca9fff6249fe47476d21ea0c28eac488000a7949651","clm_1fdcd62eda1cd35372613ac2217abf4c758c41078eafa3d30fd7808a3ea190fa","clm_25056fa832859cc129439995d0be008c159b1e980889b73c122d8f4409dac22f","clm_599228afc967fef35c60dc291c2276814232ad73d8fbc79d8e49e699d6d39bd5","clm_68a38b2ae4350b2100afd876044ff55e730f624b7828240125278b2fd51ae4fe","clm_7c4f251abe90fc57ca931b6a42d1457405259c7ab85deada8f915eeaca8e44cf","clm_919899d9296e1b3b05f46285e769ee6489f9c48b201dd96bbcb061116870b5bd","clm_c5dd72a4b88d678e304d363f3e66c996a75b77e8221c0d2e3892ca622e243e28","clm_c9a8639ad875020b5e4a7caaace4436eda1afefcb8f7853c2ca752d6d82f4026","clm_cc3fadac1a039620f9a1c7f171aa4de77e909eb14d2d484e590fc96b610f3a5a","clm_e0c6d478fe2aa23774b8688700c92310cceb9ed99265b213a2e13436287fb8ad","clm_f9d977542e326a78296791841676d7ddb29eb2d09f6f9524ebef378f6558c443"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:11:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_6e95a19acaa34bc894ac2b53a84e8f4c","id":"pg_3a579b124bc954d9b7e0277731a7a0a7","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/nicobailon-pi-boomerang-readme-md-1a5985b2d92c-277731a7a0a7.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_925c2e1ad1c957cf898dfa3a10e51300"],"title":"nicobailon/pi-boomerang/README.md @ 1a5985b2d92c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:11:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6e95a19acaa34bc894ac2b53a84e8f4c"}
